it threatens Nd6, which guards b7 and hits f7. - **If Black trades on b7:**
after ...Rbxb7 Rxb7 Rxb7, I play Rxc6. Then I have rook, knight and two pawns
against rook and three pawns, which is a big edge. - **If Black grabs f3
(...Rxf3):** I play Rxc6. That threatens Rc8+, and the b7 pawn breaks through
to promote. - **If Black plays ...Rb1:** I take with Rxb1. The rook on b8 is
blocked by my b7 pawn, so it cannot recapture, and I win the rook. } 34...
